    Confidence Level: Low

Given these findings, we have identified vulnerabilities that fall under CWEs 94 (Improper Control of Resource Identifiers), 22 (Path Traversal), and indirectly related issues under CWEs 79 (Improper Neutralization of Input During HTML Escape). However, the primary concern lies in ensuring proper memory management and input validation.

