A loop is initialized with the length of the target string `to->len`. However, this value isn't validated or checked against the maximum allowed length before use in the buffer overflow condition `(i + len > OPT_EXACT_MAXLEN)`. 

This could potentially allow an attacker to supply a maliciously crafted input that exceeds the allocated buffer size for `to`, which might enable an exploitable memory corruption attack.

