The function call `enclen(enc, p)` uses user-controlled input (`p`) as an argument. The function's documentation suggests it measures the length of a character string in the specified encoding.

However, if the encoding is not properly validated or sanitized, an attacker could exploit this to cause format string vulnerabilities or bypass checks on input lengths.


