CWEs:
- CWE-89 (SQL Injection) - High Confidence
- CWE-256 (Unprotected Storage of Credentials) - Medium to High Confidence
- CWE-22 (Path Traversal) - High Confidence
- CWE-798 (Use of Hardcoded URLs) - Low to Medium Confidence

Overall, the code needs substantial improvements in input validation, error handling, and secure coding practices.
