<analysis>
The provided Flask route appears to be secure in most regards, but the file deletion function uses an unsanitized user input (filename) directly within a string which makes it vulnerable to path traversal attacks. Attackers could manipulate the filename parameter to access unintended files or directories. This can lead to unauthorised data access and/or system manipulation vulnerabilities.

Additionally, the 'os' module is used for file removal, but without any checks in place to verify that only authorized users have permission to delete a certain video. It may be possible for an attacker to change their session username to one of another user and delete videos they should not have access to. 

Furthermore, the route does not seem to handle errors or exceptions properly. When attempting to remove/delete a file that doesn't exist, it would result in a system error message being displayed instead of preventing this situation from occurring. This could potentially provide an attacker with information about files and directories on the server. 
</analysis>

